19 Acknowledgments
******************

Emacsvox grows from Emacspeak, created by T.  V.  Raman.  Raman is the
principal original author of the inherited system, and Emacsvox
preserves his authorship and copyright notices throughout the source
where that work remains.

   The Emacsvox documentation began with the second-edition Emacspeak
user manual.  Jim Van Zandt and Jason White contributed to that manual.
Selected historical chapters remain available in the separate *note
Emacspeak Heritage: (emacsvox-heritage)Top. manual, where their original
terminology and period context can be read without confusing them with
current setup guidance.

   Thank you to everyone who has contributed code, documentation,
testing, problem reports, and practical experience to Emacspeak and
Emacsvox.  The current Emacsvox contributors continue that work while
maintaining the user guidance and generated reference in this
repository.


